headline: 
note: Fragments: a central atom and its neighbours · energies in Hartree · labels in D<sub>4h</sub> · 2 core orbitals hidden
about: **What is drawn.** The molecular levels in the middle are the calculation's own orbital energies, in Hartree. This is an unrestricted calculation: the levels are drawn at their alpha energies, and the beta electrons are matched to them by symmetry.\n\n**Fragment levels.** Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, and kept in the atom's own shell order. Its free-atom energy is given beside it.\n\n**Symmetry.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D4h; the code reported none.\n\n**Not shown.** 2 core orbitals below −18.92 Hartree.
